            <ArticleTitle>[Coronary fistula of the right ventricular outflow tract as a complication of combined transaortic-trans-right ventricular myectomy in hypertrophic obstructive cardiomyopathy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>61-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report on a patient who showed a fistula between the first septal branch of the left anterior descending coronary artery and the right ventricular outflow tract, as a complication of combined trans-aortic right ventricular myectomy for treatment of hypertrophic obstructive cardiomyopathy (HOCM).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
